# validator-fork-budget profiles scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh through scripts/fork-profile.sh, so its read set
# is the validator's whole read set plus the profiler's. The roots are derived from the validator's own `$REPO_ROOT/...`
# reads: core/, scripts/, .githooks/ and templates/ (as enforcement-map-derivations), patterns/, .claude/rules/ and
# CLAUDE.md (the I108/I121/I122/I123 corpus walks), and the committed read-set map (I118, which errs on a missing map
# in a tree that is a repository). A root left out does not fail the run: each arm's absent-root fallback forks a
# different number of times, so the fixture would measure a different program and still print PASS.
# reason: core/ is walked whole -- the profiled validator enumerates "$REPO_ROOT"/core/fixtures/*/ by content, scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh:1305, so the fork count measured is a function of every directory under core/.
# The validator under test, REQUIRED: run.sh prints the sentinel once it has located it.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
# The profiler walks up from itself for VERSION; the renderer it calls for the arm map does the same.
VERSION
scripts/
.githooks/
templates/
core/
patterns/
.claude/rules/
CLAUDE.md
.ai-dlc-fixture-readsets.tsv
